        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            For a floor, use a 1/4 inch microfiber roller cover on a good frame, or a T-bar applicator if the finish is water-based and the area is large. For furniture and table tops, the same short-nap microfiber. Avoid foam entirely.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Then slow down. Most bubble and lap-mark problems are solved not by buying a different applicator but by loading it properly, laying the finish down in unhurried passes, and resisting the urge to go back over something that has already begun to set.
          </p>
